<title>USA: CalEnergy Co Inc Q4 net, revenues higher.</title>
<headline>CalEnergy Co Inc Q4 net, revenues higher.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, Neb. 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996	1995</p>
<p> Revenues					    $190,997   $95,225</p>
<p>Income Before Provision for Income Taxes</p>
<p>   and Minority Interest			   30,564    18,935</p>
<p>Net Income Available for Common</p>
<p>   Shareholders				  $21,174(1)   $12,549</p>
<p> Net Income Per Common Share (Primary)	   0.33	0.24</p>
<p>Average Common and Common Equivalent</p>
<p>   Shares Outstanding(4)			   65,094    53,292</p>
<p>							  Twelve Months</p>
<p>							1996	    1995</p>
<p> Revenues				     $576,195	 $398,723</p>
<p>Income Before Provision for Income Taxes</p>
<p>   and Minority Interest		   135,713	   97,051</p>
<p> Income Before Preferred Dividends  92,461 (1)    $63,415 (2)</p>
<p> Preferred Dividends			  -- (3)	    1,080</p>
<p>Net Income Available for Common</p>
<p>   Shareholders				 92,461	   62,335</p>
<p> Net Income Per Common Share (Primary)    1.60	     1.25</p>
<p>Average Common and Common Equivalent</p>
<p>   Shares Outstanding(4)		    57,870	   49,971</p>
<p>(1) Includes a reduction of $1,431 for minority interest during the quarter ended December 31, 1996, reflecting the company's acquisition on December 24, 1996 of a majority interest in Northern Electric plc.</p>
<p>(2) Includes a reduction of $3,005 for minority interest during the quarter ended March 31, 1995, reflecting the full acquisition of Magma Power Co as of February 24, 1995.</p>
<p>(3) On March 15, 1995, the company exchanged all of its Series C preferred stock for $64,850 of 9.5 percent convertible debt.</p>
<p>(4) Reflects the weighted average of outstanding shares, and includes conversion of $64,850 9.5 percent convertible debt on September 20, 1996, the conversion of the $100,000 convertible subordinated debentures in September and October 1996 and the public offering of shares on February 24, 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago Newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
</text>
